        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(mattermost): wake agents from edited mentions",
        "body": "Closes #71930\n\nAI-assisted: yes. I understand the change and reviewed the source, dependency contracts, and validation below.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where Mattermost users who edited an existing message to add an `@openclaw` mention would not wake the agent because `post_edited` WebSocket events were ignored.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nMattermost edit events now enter the existing inbound post path. Transport-facing message identity stays the canonical Mattermost post id, while replay protection derives edit-specific keys from Mattermost edit metadata so the original post cannot suppress a later edited wake.\n\nEdited events bypass text batching, but the zero-delay path remains FIFO-serialized with ordinary posts from the same sender, channel, and thread. Pending ordinary posts flush first, then each edit is evaluated independently. Mention snapshots require an observed false-to-true transition and fail closed when the prior state is unknown or the sender changes. Bot and system posts are filtered before enqueueing.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers can add an `@openclaw` mention by editing an existing Mattermost message. Immediate `posted` and `post_edited` frames retain their order and wake exactly once. Formatting-only, attachment-only, replayed, other-bot, and unknown-prior-state edits do not wake the agent.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- An isolated Linux Node 24 container checked out the exact PR head and passed all 5 focused Mattermost files: 43 tests total (14 WebSocket, 10 existing routing/session, 5 existing streaming, 8 edited-mention, and 6 edited-debounce/ordering cases).\n- Public CI on the current head passes production and test types, dependency checks, lint/format, max-lines ratchet, and build.\n- The two remaining public CI failures are unrelated current-main drift: the package-acceptance workflow expectation for `allow_frozen_target_scenario_omissions`, and Android Japanese localization drift. This PR touches neither surface.\n- The 15 pre-existing inbound cases were preserved byte-for-byte when the test file was split to satisfy the max-lines gate.\n- `oxfmt --check` passed for all touched TypeScript files.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- Official Mattermost source lists both `posted` and `post_edited`, exposes `edit_at`/`update_at` on posts, and emits the edited-post WebSocket event.\n\nKnown gap: I do not have a live Mattermost tenant credential in this environment, so I cannot provide a real-provider transcript. Validation therefore uses the official Mattermost event contract plus isolated source-level WebSocket, replay, debounce, ordering, and inbound-context regression coverage.\n",
